        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US-Iran's first round of talks concludes despite Trump threatening strikes Middle East Issued on: 22/06/2026 - 11:51 High-level negotiations in Switzerland seeking a permanent end to the Iran war have ended, while technical talks will go on there for the rest of the week. US and Iranian delegation met for high-level talks following the recent signing of a \"memorandum of understanding\". However, the Iranian temporarily walked out after threats made by US President Donald Trump. Negotiators will seek to resolve some of the thornier issues between the US and Iran such as Tehran's nuclear programme and stockpiles of uranium. As Cuba's power crisis deepens, Havana's residents speak out 22/06/2026 Americas US-Iran talks 'off to strained, asymetric start' as Tehran hails success 22/06/2026 Middle East Trump threatens to strike Iran over support for Hezbollah as fighting continues in Lebanon 21/06/2026 Middle East Israeli strikes start again in Lebanon after several-hour lull, amid US-Iran talks 21/06/2026 Middle East Trump-backed de la Espriella or leftist Cepeda? Colombians elect a new president 21/06/2026 Americas Sailors trapped in Hormuz strait, dodging drones and rationing food 21/06/2026 Middle East Israel and Hezbollah trade fire, as US-Iran talks begin in Switzerland 21/06/2026 Middle East Who is Ivan Cepeda, left-wing candidate in Colombia's presidential elections? 21/06/2026 Americas Iran claims Lebanon 'main topic' at peace talks with US 21/06/2026 Middle East"
